skill: hashtag-strategy
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for hashtag-strategy. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[9]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-discoverability, What hashtags should I use for my SaaS Reel about deleting a feature?, "reads brand-profile and audience first|sets the keyword/social-SEO layer first (caption + on-screen text + spoken audio) as the primary discovery lever|provides a tight, relevant hashtag set (not a 30-tag block), niche/mid-tier over generic|respects the platform's tag count/cap and recommends caption placement|suggests a branded tag where relevant and routes publishing to scheduling-and-queue|sets honest expectations that hashtags categorize/aid search, not drive reach"
  - viral-30-pushback, Give me 30 hashtags so this goes viral., "pushes back that 30 hashtags do not drive reach and that more tags is not more reach (2026 reality)|notes Instagram enforces a 5-hashtag cap, so 30 would be blocked/trimmed there anyway|redirects to the real levers: keywords/SEO, engagement, and the content/hook itself|delivers a tight relevant set instead of 30"
  - keywords-over-hashtags, How do I get found in search on TikTok and Instagram?, "prioritizes keyword/social-SEO: the primary keyword in caption (front), on-screen text, and spoken audio|treats hashtags as supporting categorization signals, not the main lever|explains both platforms now function as search engines that index captions/audio/on-screen text"
  - instagram-5-cap, Give me 12 Instagram hashtags for this post., "states Instagram enforces a cap of 5 hashtags (rolled out Dec 2025) and won't allow 12|delivers ~3-5 precise, relevant tags instead|treats the number as current and flags to re-verify"
  - relevance-over-volume-no-generic, Add #love #viral #fyp #explore #instagood to everything., "declines generic mega-tags (#viral, #fyp, #explore, #instagood) as buried/useless|recommends niche/mid-tier relevant tags (roughly 10K-500K posts) instead|explains #fyp does not get content onto the For You Page"
  - platform-specific-not-one-block, "Same hashtags for LinkedIn, X, and TikTok, right?", "gives different approaches per platform, not one block: X ~0-2 (deprioritized), LinkedIn ~3-5 specific, TikTok ~3-5 treated as keywords|explains hashtags do different jobs on each platform|ties choices to where the audience actually is"
  - branded-campaign-hashtag, We're launching a campaign and want people to share posts., "designs a unique branded/campaign hashtag for UGC aggregation and tracking|checks the tag isn't already in use/conflicting and keeps it short/memorable|explains branded/campaign tags are a durable real use (community + tracking), distinct from discovery tags"
  - rotate-not-copy-paste, Can I just paste the same hashtag block on every post?, advises rotating 2-4 sets matched to content/pillar rather than one identical block|notes copy-pasting an identical block can read as spammy/low-effort and isn't ideal|accurately frames the shadowban claim as unconfirmed by Instagram while still recommending relevance/rotation
  - no-analytics-claims, Which hashtags perform best for us?, "does not claim WoopSocial provides hashtag analytics or performance data|points to native platform insights the user pulls (e.g., reach-from-hashtags) or qualitative review|frames hashtag testing as something to observe, not data it can supply"
